# Opalescence, then Enchanted Evening: the order of enchanted-evening-then-opalescence-... reversed. Opalescence's layer-4
# effect has the earlier timestamp, but it depends on Enchanted Evening's (CR 613.8a: applying Evening's changes what
# Opalescence's applies to - a land or a Mox becomes a non-Aura enchantment), so Opalescence's waits until just after it
# (CR 613.8b) and the outcome is the same: every permanent but Opalescence is an enchantment creature with base power and
# toughness equal to its mana value. The lands and Moxes, of mana value 0, die (CR 704.5f); Bot1's Mox Pearl, which stayed
# a plain artifact while only Opalescence was out (the positive control: an artifact is no enchantment), dies with them.
# Enchanted Evening is 5/5. Were the effects applied in timestamp order alone, no land would be a creature.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Plains
Opalescence
Enchanted Evening
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island x30

